From c621a49b122f304058fb96639d0afa35b3dd4d46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_sched_fixed <>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:36:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] apps/examples/testcase: add scheduling scenario test harness
 and round-robin scenarios

Adds a scenario test tier alongside the existing API level tc_ and itc_
tests.  Scenario tests assert on scheduler behaviour under a controlled
workload instead of on API return values, which is the only way to cover a
subsystem whose specification is a statement about which task runs when.

stc_sched_common provides the shared harness: a non-blocking spin worker
whose progress counter is isolated in its own cache line, a window runner
that discards a warm-up period, applies the load, snapshots the counters and
verifies every worker exited, and the oracles used to turn those counters
into a verdict.  The harness raises its own priority above the workload for
the duration so it never competes with what it is measuring.  Work counters
are used rather than elapsed time because the system tick is 1 ms while
CONFIG_RR_INTERVAL is typically 10 ms, which leaves too little headroom for
a timing based oracle.

Among the oracles is stc_min_range(), a minimum over a range of workers
rather than over all of them.  Scenarios that deliberately starve one worker
need to exclude it, or the assertion states the opposite of the property
under test.

stc_sched_rr implements the first three scenarios:

  SCN-RR-01  ncpus + 1 unpinned equal priority tasks.  The surplus task can
             only ever be admitted by round-robin rotation, so it records no
             work at all if rotation does not happen.
  SCN-RR-02  three equal priority tasks pinned to CPU0, sharing one run
             queue, where rotation is a plain cycle through one priority
             band and the spread should be tight.
  SCN-RR-03  two equal priority tasks pinned to the highest numbered CPU.
             Where the system tick is enabled on CPU0 only, the timeslice
             check for every other CPU is performed remotely from inside
             CPU0's critical section, and a predicate there that asks about
             the wrong CPU suppresses rotation on the secondary CPU
             permanently while CPU0 keeps rotating.  RR-01 can mask that;
             pinning isolates it.

Each scenario states its oracle as two separate assertions, a hard
correctness one that can never be flaky and a fairness one carrying a
tolerance, so a red suite immediately identifies which kind broke.

Gated by CONFIG_STC_KERNEL_SCHED, default n and deliberately not selected by
TC_KN_ALL: the windows are seconds long and belong in a nightly run rather
than a per commit gate.  Builds clean for both SMP and non-SMP; SCN-RR-03
skips on single core configurations.
---
